# The network of "BGP sessions and policy": the dual-homed shop.
#
#   office  198.51.100.10  \
#   shopweb 198.51.100.200  -- shop -- edge (AS 65001, the shop's router)
#                                       /                \
#                     ispa (AS 65010, ISP A)       ispb (AS 65020, ISP B)
#                               |                         |
#                     transit (AS 65030)                  |
#                               \                         |
#                                 cloud (AS 65100) -------
#                                   |     (and a private link, "vpn", to edge)
#                                  web 203.0.113.10 (a web server)
#
# Each router's interfaces are named after what is at the far end of the
# cable: on edge, "ispa" goes to ISP A, "ispb" to ISP B and "lan" to the
# shop's switch. The ISPs, the transit network and the cloud are scenery,
# configured and saved; edge is the learner's. Addresses come from the
# documentation ranges (RFC 5737) and AS numbers from the private range
# (RFC 6996), so nothing here is anybody's real network.
machine office
machine shopweb
machine web
machine edge router
machine ispa router
machine ispb router
machine transit router
machine cloud router

lan shop office:eth0=198.51.100.10/24 shopweb:eth0=198.51.100.200/24 edge:lan=198.51.100.1/24
link edge:ispa=192.0.2.1/30 ispa:edge=192.0.2.2/30
link edge:ispb=192.0.2.5/30 ispb:edge=192.0.2.6/30
link ispa:transit=192.0.2.9/30 transit:ispa=192.0.2.10/30
link transit:cloud=192.0.2.13/30 cloud:transit=192.0.2.14/30
link ispb:cloud=192.0.2.17/30 cloud:ispb=192.0.2.18/30
link cloud:web=203.0.113.1/24 web:eth0=203.0.113.10/24
# The shop's new private link to the cloud: a stand-in for a VPN tunnel with
# BGP over it, addressed like one (a /30 from 169.254.0.0/16).
link edge:vpn=169.254.30.1/30 cloud:vpn=169.254.30.2/30

route office default via 198.51.100.1
route shopweb default via 198.51.100.1
route web default via 203.0.113.1
# ISP B keeps a route for the top half of the shop's addresses, pointing at
# the shop, and by a slip announces it to the shop as well (its routers
# hand kernel routes inside the shop's block to their customer).
route ispb 198.51.100.128/25 via 192.0.2.5

run edge frr
run ispa frr
run ispb frr
run transit frr
run cloud frr
run web nginx
run shopweb nginx
